  "description": "Follows the Mahabharata beyond victory: the women’s laments, Kunti’s revelation, Yudhishthira’s wish to renounce the throne and Bhishma’s instruction on governing after catastrophe. Examines the horse sacrifice, competing measures of generosity, the elders’ departure, Krishna’s death and the final journey and afterlife tests, then considers the epic’s transmission and the limits of its historical evidence.",
